@nsobid-41EAE379C103E9A512CFA931BA400E938B3B7C55

# Captain Toad Treasure Tracker 1.4.2 - 2560x1440 resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Renders at 2560x1440 in both docked and handheld mode.
//
// The engine keeps three sizes: the display buffer the nn::vi layer
// presents, two frame buffers the scene is composed into (docked and
// handheld, each with a virtual size and a texture size), and the 3D render
// size from al::GraphicsStressDirector::getBufferSizeX/Y, which follows the
// dynamic quality controller and is clamped to the frame buffer's virtual
// size. Stock docked play keeps all of them at 1920x1080; handheld keeps
// the 1920x1080 virtual size and shrinks the texture and render to
// 1280x720.
//
// Every one of those sizes is raised to 2560x1440, so the render, the
// viewports laid over it and the textures it resolves into stay in the
// same 1:1 relation as stock docked play. Rendering above the virtual size
// is not a layout the engine supports. The two frame buffers share one
// allocation, so they must stay the same size. Both size getters return
// the fixed size, which also stops the dynamic quality controller from
// lowering it.
//
// Every render target, including the cascaded shadow map, comes from the
// agl::utl::DynamicTextureAllocator pool (100 MB at 1080p) inside AglHeap
// (170 MB). The pool is raised to 640 MB, which also leaves room for the
// [Shadow Resolution 4096] mod, and AglHeap grows by the same amount. The
// sead root heap (2379 MB) grows by the pool increase plus the larger
// display, frame buffer and screen capture textures, so the scene heaps
// keep their stock headroom. The result still fits the 3 GB memory heap
// the game requests at boot, so the default 4 GiB DRAM setting is enough.
//
// This mod OWNS the pool and heap offsets below; do not duplicate them in
// another enabled mod.

@enabled
// Display buffer size in the sead::GameFrameworkNx::CreateArg (was 1920x1080).
0025E084 084081D2   // MOVZ X8,#2560
0025E090 08B4C0F2   // MOVK X8,#1440,LSL#32
// sead::GameFrameworkNx::initializeGraphicsSystem logical frame buffer size.
0025E0CC 08A4A8D2   // MOVZ X8,#0x4520,LSL#16 = 2560.0f (was 1920.0f)
0025E0D8 8896E8F2   // MOVK X8,#0x44B4,LSL#48 = 1440.0f (was 1080.0f)
// al::GameFrameworkNx::initAgl frame buffers.
0025E0F4 03B48052   // MOVZ W3,#1440 (was 1080, virtual height)
0025E0FC 06408152   // MOVZ W6,#2560 (was 1280, handheld texture)
0025E100 07B48052   // MOVZ W7,#1440 (was 720, handheld texture)
0025E104 02408152   // MOVZ W2,#2560 (was 1920, virtual width)
0025E108 04408152   // MOVZ W4,#2560 (was 1920, docked texture)
0025E110 05B48052   // MOVZ W5,#1440 (was MOV W5,W3 = 1080, docked texture)
// al::GraphicsStressDirector::getBufferSizeX / getBufferSizeY.
002D7210 00408152   // MOVZ W0,#2560
002D7214 C0035FD6   // RET
002D72E0 00B48052   // MOVZ W0,#1440
002D72E4 C0035FD6   // RET
// agl::InitArg DynamicTextureAllocator pool and the AglHeap holding it.
0040C240 0800A552   // MOVZ W8,#0x2800,LSL#16 = 640 MB (was 100 MB)
0040C208 008CA552   // MOVZ W0,#0x2C60,LSL#16 = 710 MB (was 170 MB)
// sead root heap in ApplicationFunction::initialize.
0025E8E4 0836B752   // MOVZ W8,#0xB9B0,LSL#16 = 2971 MB (was 2379 MB)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Captain Toad Treasure Tracker 1.4.2
// (al + agl + sead, NVN). The retail build keeps its symbol table; every
// site was located by symbol and byte-verified against the IDB before
// being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
